{
  "title": "13: al-Ra'd الرعد",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nالٓمّٓرٰ تِلْكَ اٰيٰتُ الْكِتٰبِؕ وَالَّذِىْۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكَ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ الْحَقُّ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(1)\nALAAMMAARAA TILKA AAYAATUL AL-KETAABE WAL LAZEE UNZELA ELAYKA MIN RABBEKA HAQQO LAAKINNAL AKSARAN NAASE LAA YOAMENOONA.\nA.L.M.R. These are the signs (or verses) of the Book: that which hath been revealed unto thee from thy Lord is the Truth; but most men believe not. \nاَللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ رَفَعَ السَّمٰوٰتِ بِغَيْرِ عَمَدٍ تَرَوْنَهَا ثُمَّ اسْتَوٰى عَلَى الْعَرْشِ وَسَخَّرَ الشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَؕ كُلٌّ يَّجْرِىْ لِاَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّىؕ يُدَبِّرُ الْاَمْرَ يُفَصِّلُ الْاٰيٰتِ لَعَلَّكُمْ بِلِقَآءِ رَبِّكُمْ تُوْقِنُوْنَ‏(2)\nALLAAHO LAZEE RAFAA’A SAMAAWAATE BEGHAYRIL A’MADIM TARAWNAHAA SUMMA TAWAA A’LAL A’RSHIL SAKHKHARASH SHAMSA WAL QAMARA KULLUL YYAJREAA LE-ELAA MOSAMMAA YUDABBERU AMRA YUFASSELU AAYAATE LA-A’LLAKUM BELEQAAE RABBEKUM TOOQENOONA.\nAllah is He Who raised the heavens without any pillars that ye can see; is firmly established on the throne (of authority); He has subjected the sun and the moon (to his Law)! Each one runs (its course) for a term appointed. He doth regulate all affairs, explaining the signs in detail, that ye may believe with certainty in the meeting with your Lord. \nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ مَدَّ الْاَرْضَ وَجَعَلَ فِيْهَا رَوَاسِىَ وَاَنْهٰرًا ؕ وَمِنْ كُلِّ الثَّمَرٰتِ جَعَلَ فِيْهَا زَوْجَيْنِ اثْنَيْنِ يُغْشِى الَّيْلَ النَّهَارَ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يَّتَفَكَّرُوْنَ‏(3)\nWA HOWA LAZEE MADDA ARZA WA FEEHAA JA-A’LA WA KHELAALAHAA WA MIN KULLE SAMARAATE JA-A’LA FEEHAA ZAWJAYNE NAYNE YUGHSHEAA LAYLA NAHAARA INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEQAWMINY YATAFAKKAROON.\nAnd it is He who spread out the earth, and set thereon mountains standing firm and (flowing) rivers: and fruit of every kind He made in pairs, two and two: He draweth the night as a veil o'er the Day. Behold, verily in these things there are signs for those who consider! \nوَ فِى الْاَرْضِ قِطَعٌ مُّتَجٰوِرٰتٌ وَّجَنّٰتٌ مِّنْ اَعْنَابٍ وَّزَرْعٌ وَّنَخِيْلٌ صِنْوَانٌ وَّغَيْرُ صِنْوَانٍ يُّسْقٰى بِمَآءٍ وَّاحِدٍ وَنُفَضِّلُ بَعْضَهَا عَلٰى بَعْضٍ فِى الْاُكُلِؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يَّعْقِلُوْنَ‏(4)\nWA FIL ARZE QETAA’UN MMUTAJAAWERAATUN WWAJANNAATUN MIN AAA’NAABIN WWAZARA’UN WWANAKHEELUN SENWAANUN WWAGHAYRU SENWAANIN YYUSQAA BE-MAAA-IM WAAHEDIN WANUFAZZELU BAA’ZAHAA A’LAA ELAA FIL AL-AUKULE INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEQAWMINY YA’QELOON.\nAnd in the earth are tracts (diverse though) neighbouring, and gardens of vines and fields sown with corn, and palm trees - growing out of single roots or otherwise: watered with the same water, yet some of them We make more excellent than others to eat. Behold, verily in these things there are signs for those who understand! \nوَ اِنْ تَعْجَبْ فَعَجَبٌ قَوْلُهُمْ ءَاِذَا كُنَّا تُرٰبًا ءَاِنَّا لَفِىْ خَلْقٍ جَدِيْدٍ  ؕ اُولٰۤئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِرَبِّهِمْۚ وَاُولٰۤئِكَ الْاَغْلٰلُ فِىْۤ اَعْنَاقِهِمْۚ وَاُولٰۤئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ النَّارِۚ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(5)\nWA IN TAA’JAB FAA’AJABUN QAWLOHUM A-EZAA KUNNAA TORAABAWN A-INNAA LAFEE KHALQIN JADEEDIN AOOLAAEKA LAZEENA KAFAROO BE-RABBEHIM WAAWLAAEKA AL-AAGHLAALU FEE AAA’NAAQEHEM WAAWLAAEKA ASHAABUN NAAR HUM FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\nIf thou dost marvel (at their want of faith), strange is their saying: “When we are (actually) dust, shall we indeed then be in a creation renewed?” They are those who deny their Lord! They are those round whose necks will be yokes (of servitude): they will be Companions of the Fire, to dwell therein (for aye)! \nوَيَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَكَ بِالسَّيِّئَةِ قَبْلَ الْحَسَنَةِ وَقَدْ خَلَتْ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمُ الْمَثُلٰتُؕ وَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَذُوْ مَغْفِرَةٍ لِّلنَّاسِ عَلٰى ظُلْمِهِمْۚ وَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَشَدِيْدُ الْعِقَابِ‏(6)\nWA YASTA’JELOONAKA BIS-SAYYEATE QABLA HASANATE WA QAD KHALAT MIN QABLEHEMU AL-MASULAATU WA INNA RABBAKA LAZOO MAGHFERATIN LIN-NAASE A’LAA ZULMEHEM WA INNA RABBAKA LASHADEEDU E’QAAB.\nThey ask thee to hasten on the evil in preference to the good: Yet have come to pass, before them, (many) exemplary punishments! But verily thy Lord is full of forgiveness for mankind for their wrong-doing, and verily thy Lord is (also) strict in punishment. \nوَيَقُوْلُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَوْلَاۤ اُنْزِلَ عَلَيْهِ اٰيَةٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّهٖؕ اِنَّمَاۤ اَنْتَ مُنْذِرٌ وَّ لِكُلِّ قَوْمٍ هَادٍ‏(7)\nWA YAQOOLO LAZEENA KAFAROO LAWLAA UNZELA A’LAYHE TAA-TEENAA MIN RABBEH INNAMAA ANTA MUNZERUN WA LEKULLIM QAWMIN HAADIN.\nAnd the Unbelievers say: “Why is not a sign sent down to him from his Lord?” But thou art truly a warner, and to every people a guide. \nاَللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُ مَا تَحْمِلُ كُلُّ اُنْثٰى وَمَا تَغِيْضُ الْاَرْحَامُ وَمَا تَزْدَادُ ؕ وَكُلُّ شَىْءٍ عِنْدَهٗ بِمِقْدَارٍ‏(8)\nALLAAHO YA’LAMO MAA TAHMELO KULLO UNSAA WA MAA TAGHEEZU AL-AARHAAMU WA MAA TAZDAADU WA KULLO SHAY-IN I’NDAHU BEMEQDAARIN.\nAllah doth know what every female (womb) doth bear, by how much the wombs fall short (of their time or number) or do exceed. Every single thing is before His sight, in (due) proportion. \nعٰلِمُ الْغَيْبِ وَالشَّهَادَةِ الْكَبِيْرُ الْمُتَعَالِ‏(9)\nA’ALEMUL GHAYBE WASH SHAHAADATE AL-KABEERU AL-MUTAA’AALE.\nHe knoweth the unseen and that which is open: He is the Great, the Most High. \nسَوَآءٌ مِّنْكُمْ مَّنْ اَسَرَّ الْقَوْلَ وَ مَنْ جَهَرَ بِهٖ وَمَنْ هُوَ مُسْتَخْفٍۢ بِالَّيْلِ وَسَارِبٌۢ بِالنَّهَارِ‏(10)\nSAWAAA-UN MINKUM MAN AASARRA QAWLA WA MAN JAHARA BEHI WA MAN HOWA MUSTAKHFIN BIL-LAYLE WASAAREBUN BEALNNAHAARE.\nIt is the same (to Him) whether any of you conceal his speech or declare it openly; whether he lie hid by night or walk forth freely by day. \nلَهٗ مُعَقِّبٰتٌ مِّنْۢ بَيْنِ يَدَيْهِ وَمِنْ خَلْفِهٖ يَحْفَظُوْنَهٗ مِنْ اَمْرِ اللّٰهِؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُغَيِّرُ مَا بِقَوْمٍ حَتّٰى يُغَيِّرُوْا مَا بِاَنْفُسِهِمْؕ وَاِذَاۤ اَرَادَ اللّٰهُ بِقَوْمٍ سُوْۤءًا فَلَا مَرَدَّ لَهٗۚ وَمَا لَهُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِهٖ مِنْ وَّالٍ‏(11)\nLAHU MUA’AQQEBAATUN MIN BAYNE YADAYHE WA MIN KHALFEH YAHFAZOONAH MIN AMRE LAAH INNAL LAAHA LAA YUGHAYRU MAA BE-QAWMIN HATTAA YUGHAYROOA MAA BEAANFUSEHEM WA EZAA ARAADA LAAHO BE-QAWMIN SOOAN FALAA MARADDA LAHU WA MAA LAHUM MIN DOONEHI MIN WWAALIN.\nFor each (such person) there are (angels) in succession, before and behind him: They guard him by command of Allah. Allah does not change a people's lot unless they change what is in their hearts. But when (once) Allah willeth a people's punishment, there can be no turning it back, nor will they find, besides Him, any to protect. \nهُوَ الَّذِىْ يُرِيْكُمُ الْبَرْقَ خَوْفًا وَّطَمَعًا وَّيُنْشِئُ السَّحَابَ الثِّقَالَۚ‏(12)\nHOWA LAZEE AAYAATEHI YOREEKOMUL BARQA KHAWFANW WWAYUNSHEU AS-SAHAABA AS-SEQAALA.\nIt is He Who doth show you the lightning, by way both of fear and of hope: It is He Who doth raise up the clouds, heavy with (fertilising) rain! \nوَيُسَبِّحُ الرَّعْدُ بِحَمْدِهٖ وَالْمَلٰۤئِكَةُ مِنْ خِيْفَتِهٖ ۚ وَيُرْسِلُ الصَّوَاعِقَ فَيُصِيْبُ بِهَا مَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَهُمْ يُجَادِلُوْنَ فِى اللّٰهۚ ِ وَهُوَ شَدِيْدُ الْمِحَالِؕ‏(13)\nWA YOSABBEHO AR-RAA’DU BEHAMDEH WAL MALAAEKATU MIN KHEEFATEH WA YURSELUR AS-SAWAAE’EQA FAYUSEEBU BEHAA MAN YASHAAA-O WA HUM YUJAADELOONA FIL AL-LAAH WA HOWA SHADEEDUL AL-MEHAALE.\nNay, thunder repeateth His praises, and so do the angels, with awe: He flingeth the loud-voiced thunder-bolts, and therewith He striketh whomsoever He will..yet these (are the men) who (dare to) dispute about Allah, with the strength of His power (supreme)! \nلَهٗ دَعْوَةُ الْحَقِّؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ يَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ لَا يَسْتَجِيْبُوْنَ لَهُمْ بِشَىْءٍ اِلَّا كَبَاسِطِ كَفَّيْهِ اِلَى الْمَآءِ لِيَبْلُغَ فَاهُ وَمَا هُوَ بِبَالِغِهٖؕ وَمَا دُعَآءُ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ اِلَّا فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ‏(14)\nLAHU DAA’WATU HAQQ WAL LAZEENA YAD-O’ONA MIN DOONEHI LAA YASTAJEEBOONA LAHUM BE-SHAY-IM ILLAA KABAASETE KAFFAYHE ELAL AL-MAAE LE-HATTAA FAAHU WA MAA HOWA BEBAALEGHEH WA MAA DUA’AAU KAAFEREEN ILLAA FEE ZALAALIM.\nFor Him (alone) is prayer in Truth: any others that they call upon besides Him hear them no more than if they were to stretch forth their hands for water to reach their mouths but it reaches them not: for the prayer of those without Faith is nothing but (futile) wandering (in the mind). \nوَلِلّٰهِ يَسْجُدُ مَنْ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ طَوْعًا وَّكَرْهًا وَّظِلٰلُهُمْ بِالْغُدُوِّ وَالْاٰصَالِ ۩‏(15)\nLILLAAHE YASJUDU MAN FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE TEYAA WWAKARHAN WWAZELAALUHUM BIL-GHUDOO WAL AAASAALE.\nWhatever beings there are in the heavens and the earth do prostrate themselves to Allah (Acknowledging subjection), with good-will or in spite of themselves: so do their shadows in the morning and evenings. [۩] \nقُلْ مَنْ رَّبُّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ قُلِ اللّٰهُؕ قُلْ اَفَاتَّخَذْتُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِهٖۤ اَوْلِيَآءَ لَا يَمْلِكُوْنَ لِاَنْفُسِهِمْ نَفْعًا وَّلَا ضَرًّاؕ قُلْ هَلْ يَسْتَوِى الْاَعْمٰى وَالْبَصِيْرُ ۙ اَمْ هَلْ تَسْتَوِى الظُّلُمٰتُ وَالنُّوْرُ ۚ اَمْ جَعَلُوْا لِلّٰهِ شُرَكَآءَ خَلَقُوْا كَخَلْقِهٖ فَتَشَابَهَ الْخَلْقُ عَلَيْهِمْؕ قُلِ اللّٰهُ خَالِقُ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَّهُوَ الْوَاحِدُ الْقَهَّارُ‏(16)\nQUL MAN RRABBU SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ QOLIL LAAH QUL AAFAATTAKHAZTUM MIN DOONEHI AAWLEEAAAA LAA YAMLEKOONA LE-ANFOSEHIM BEKUM WA LAA ZARRAN QUL HAL YASTAWEAA A-A’MAA WAL BASEERU AM HAL LAA AZ-ZULUMAATU WAALNNOORU AM JAA’ALOOA LILLAAHE SHORA-KAAA-A KHALAQOOA KAKHALQEH FATASHAABAHA AL-KHALQU WA QOLIL LAAHO KHAALEQU KULLE SHAY-IN WA AL-WAAHEDU AL-QAHHAARU.\n\nاَنْزَلَ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً فَسَالَتْ اَوْدِيَةٌۢ بِقَدَرِهَا فَاحْتَمَلَ السَّيْلُ زَبَدًا رَّابِيًا ؕ وَمِمَّا يُوْقِدُوْنَ عَلَيْهِ فِى النَّارِ ابْتِغَآءَ حِلْيَةٍ اَوْ مَتَاعٍ زَبَدٌ مِّثْلُهٗ ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يَضْرِبُ اللّٰهُ الْحَقَّ وَالْبَاطِلَ ؕ  فَاَمَّا الزَّبَدُ فَيَذْهَبُ جُفَآءً ۚ وَاَمَّا مَا يَنْفَعُ النَّاسَ فَيَمْكُثُ فِى الْاَرْضِؕ كَذٰلِكَ يَضْرِبُ اللّٰهُ الْاَمْثَالَؕ‏(17)\nANZALAL MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN FASAALAT AAWDEETUN BEQADAREHAA FAAHTAMALA AS-SAYLU ZABADAN RRAABEEA WA MIMMAA YOOQEDOONA A’LAYHE FIL NAAR TEGHAAA-A HELYATIN AW MATAAA’IN ZABADUN MMESLUH KAZAALEKA YAZREBU LAAHO HAQQA WAL BAATELA FA-AMMAA AZ-ZABADU FAYAZHABU JUFAAAN WA AMMAA MAA YANFAU’N NAASA FAYAMKUSU FIL ARZ KAZAALEKA YAZREBU LAAHO AL-AAMSAALA.\nSay: “Who is the Lord and Sustainer of the heavens and the earth?” Say: “(It is) Allah.” Say: “Do ye then take (for worship) protectors other than Him, such as have no power either for good or for harm to themselves?” Say: “Are the blind equal with those who see? Or the depths of darkness equal with light?” Or do they assign to Allah partners who have created (anything) as He has created, so that the creation seemed to them similar? Say: “Allah is the Creator of all things: He is the One, the Supreme and Irresistible.” \nلِلَّذِيْنَ اسْتَجَابُوْا لِرَبِّهِمُ الْحُسْنٰىؔؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ لَمْ يَسْتَجِيْبُوْا لَهٗ لَوْ اَنَّ لَهُمْ مَّا فِى الْاَرْضِ جَمِيْعًا وَّمِثْلَهٗ مَعَهٗ لَافْتَدَوْا بِهٖؕ اُولٰۤئِكَ لَهُمْ سُوْۤءُ الْحِسَابِ ۙ وَمَاْوٰٮهُمْ جَهَنَّمُؕ وَبِئْسَ الْمِهَادُ‏(18)\nLILLAZEENA ASTAJAABOOA LERABBEHEMU AL-HUSNAA WAL LAZEENA LAM YASTAJEEBOO LAHU LAW ANNAL LAHUM MAA FIL ARZE JAMEE-A’A WWAMESLAH MA-A’HU LAAFTADAWA BEH AOOLAAEKA LAHUM SOOU HESAAB WAMAAWAAHUM JAHANNAM WA WA BEASAL MEHAAD.\nHe sends down water from the skies, and the channels flow, each according to its measure: But the torrent bears away to foam that mounts up to the surface. Even so, from that (ore) which they heat in the fire, to make ornaments or utensils therewith, there is a scum likewise. Thus doth Allah (by parables) show forth Truth and Vanity. For the scum disappears like forth cast out; while that which is for the good of mankind remains on the earth. Thus doth Allah set forth parables. \nاَفَمَنْ يَّعْلَمُ اَنَّمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكَ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ الْحَقُّ كَمَنْ هُوَ اَعْمٰىؕ اِنَّمَا يَتَذَكَّرُ اُولُوا الْاَلْبَابِۙ‏(19)\nAFAMAWN YYAA’LAMU ANNAMAA UNZELA ELAYKA MIN RABBEKA HAQQO KAMAM HOWA AAA’MAA INNAMAA YATAZAKKARU ULUL ULIL ALBAABE.\nFor those who respond to their Lord, are (all) good things. But those who respond not to Him, Even if they had all that is in the heavens and on earth, and as much more, (in vain) would they offer it for ransom. For them will the reckoning be terrible: their abode will be Hell, what a bed of misery! \nالَّذِيْنَ يُوْفُوْنَ بِعَهْدِ اللّٰهِ وَلَا يَنْقُضُوْنَ الْمِيْثَاقَۙ‏(20)\nLAZEENA YOOFOONA BEA’AHDE LAAHE WA LAA YANQOZOONA AL-MEESAAQA.\nIs then one who doth know that that which hath been revealed unto thee from thy Lord is the Truth, like one who is blind? It is those who are endued with understanding that receive admonition;- \nوَالَّذِيْنَ يَصِلُوْنَ مَاۤ اَمَرَ اللّٰهُ بِهٖۤ اَنْ يُّوْصَلَ وَيَخْشَوْنَ رَبَّهُمْ وَ يَخَافُوْنَ سُوْۤءَ الْحِسَابِؕ‏(21)\nWAL LAZEENA YASELOONA MAA AMARAL LAAHO BEHI AN YOOSALA WA YAKHSHAWNA RABBAHUM WA YAKHAAFOONA SOOA AL-HESAABE.\nThose who fulfil the covenant of Allah and fail not in their plighted word; \nوَالَّذِيْنَ صَبَرُوا ابْتِغَآءَ وَجْهِ رَبِّهِمْ وَاَقَامُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَاَنْفَقُوْا مِمَّا رَزَقْنٰهُمْ سِرًّا وَّعَلَانِيَةً وَّيَدْرَءُوْنَ بِالْحَسَنَةِ السَّيِّئَةَ اُولٰۤئِكَ لَهُمْ عُقْبَى الدَّارِۙ‏(22)\nWAL LAZEENA SABAROOA TEGHAAA-A WAJHIL RABBEHIM WA AQAAMUS SALAATA WA ANFAQOO MIMMAA RAZAQNAAHUM SIRRAN WA A’LAANEYATAN WWAYADRAOONA BIL-HASANATE SAYYEATE AOOLAAEKA LAHUM U’UQBAA AD-DAARE.\nThose who join together those things which Allah hath commanded to be joined, hold their Lord in awe, and fear the terrible reckoning; \nجَنّٰتُ عَدْنٍ يَّدْخُلُوْنَهَا وَمَنْ صَلَحَ مِنْ اٰبَآئِهِمْ وَاَزْوَاجِهِمْ وَذُرِّيّٰتِهِمْ وَالْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ يَدْخُلُوْنَ عَلَيْهِمْ مِّنْ كُلِّ بَابٍۚ‏(23)\nJANNAATU A’ADNIN YYADKHULOONAHAA WA MAN SALAHA MIN AAABAAEHEM WA AZWAAJEHIM WAZURREETEHEM WAL MALAAA-EKATO YADKHOLOONA A’LAYHIM MIN KULLE BAABIN.\nThose who patiently persevere, seeking the countenance of their Lord; Establish regular prayers; spend, out of (the gifts) We have bestowed for their sustenance, secretly and openly; and turn off Evil with good: for such there is the final attainment of the (eternal) home, \nسَلٰمٌ عَلَيْكُمْ بِمَا صَبَرْتُمْ فَنِعْمَ عُقْبَى الدَّارِؕ‏(24)\nSALAAMUN A’LAYKUM BEMAA SABARTUM FA NE’MA U’UQBAA DAAR.\nGardens of perpetual bliss: they shall enter there, as well as the righteous among their fathers, their spouses, and their offspring: and angels shall enter unto them from every gate (with the salutation): \nوَالَّذِيْنَ يَنْقُضُوْنَ عَهْدَ اللّٰهِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مِيْثَاقِهٖ وَيَقْطَعُوْنَ مَاۤ اَمَرَ اللّٰهُ بِهٖۤ اَنْ يُّوْصَلَ وَيُفْسِدُوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِۙ اُولٰۤئِكَ لَهُمُ اللَّعْنَةُ وَلَهُمْ سُوْۤءُ الدَّارِ‏(25)\nWAL LAZEENA YANQOZOONA A’HDAL LAAHE MIN BA’DE MEESAAQEH WA YAQTA-O’ONA MAA AMARAL LAAHO BEHI AN YOOSALA WA YUFSEDOONA FIL ARZE AOOLAAEKA LAHOMUL AL-LAA’NATU WA LAHUM SOOU AD-DAARE.\n“Peace unto you for that ye persevered in patience! Now how excellent is the final home!” \nاَللّٰهُ يَبْسُطُ الرِّزْقَ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَقْدِرُؕ وَفَرِحُوْا بِالْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا ؕ وَمَا الْحَيٰوةُ الدُّنْيَا فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ اِلَّا مَتَاعٌ‏(26)\nALLAAHO YABSOTUR RIZQA LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O WA YAQDER WA FAREHOO BE-HAYAATID DUNYAA WA MAA HAYAATUD DUNYAA FIL AAKHERATE ILLAA LIL-MOTAALLAQAATE.\nBut those who break the Covenant of Allah, after having plighted their word thereto, and cut asunder those things which Allah has commanded to be joined, and work mischief in the land;- on them is the curse; for them is the terrible home! \nوَيَقُوْلُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَوْلَاۤ اُنْزِلَ عَلَيْهِ اٰيَةٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّهٖؕ قُلْ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُضِلُّ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَهْدِىْۤ اِلَيْهِ مَنْ اَنَابَ ۖ ۚ‏(27)\nWA YAQOOLO LAZEENA KAFAROO LAWLAA UNZELA A’LAYHE TAA-TEENAA MIN RABBEH QUL INNAL LAAHA YOZILLO MAN YASHAAA-O WA YAHDEE ELAYHE MAN AANAABA.\nAllah doth enlarge, or grant by (strict) measure, the sustenance (which He giveth) to whomso He pleaseth. (The wordly) rejoice in the life of this world: But the life of this world is but little comfort in the Hereafter. \nاَلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَتَطْمَئِنُّ قُلُوْبُهُمْ بِذِكْرِ اللّٰهِ ؕ اَلَا بِذِكْرِ اللّٰهِ تَطْمَئِنُّ الْقُلُوْبُ ؕ‏(28)\nLAZEENA AAMANOO WATATMAENNU QULOOBUHUM BE-ELAA LAAHE ALAA BE-ELAA LAAHE TATMAENNU BALAGHATIL.\nThe Unbelievers say: “Why is not a sign sent down to him from his Lord?” Say: “Truly Allah leaveth, to stray, whom He will; But He guideth to Himself those who turn to Him in penitence, \nاَلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ طُوْبٰى لَهُمْ وَحُسْنُ مَاٰبٍ‏(29)\nLAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE TOOBAA LAHUM WAHUSNU MAABIN.\n“Those who believe, and whose hearts find satisfaction in the remembrance of Allah: for without doubt in the remembrance of Allah do hearts find satisfaction. \nكَذٰلِكَ اَرْسَلْنٰكَ فِىْۤ اُمَّةٍ قَدْ خَلَتْ مِنْ قَبْلِهَاۤ اُمَمٌ لِّتَتْلُوَا۟ عَلَيْهِمُ الَّذِىْۤ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ وَ هُمْ يَكْفُرُوْنَ بِالرَّحْمٰنِؕ قُلْ هُوَ رَبِّىْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَۚ عَلَيْهِ تَوَكَّلْتُ وَاِلَيْهِ مَتَابِ‏(30)\nKAZAALEKA ARSALNAAKA FEE UMMATIN QAD KHALAT MIN QABLEHAA OMAMUM LLETATLOOA A’LAYHEMUL LAZEE AAWHAYNAA ELAYKA WA HUM YAKFOROON BE-RAHMAAN QUL HOWA RABBEE LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA A’LAYHE TAWAKKALTU WA ELAYHE MATAABE.\n“For those who believe and work righteousness, is (every) blessedness, and a beautiful place of (final) return.” \nوَلَوْ اَنَّ قُرْاٰنًا سُيِّرَتْ بِهِ الْجِبَالُ اَوْ قُطِّعَتْ بِهِ الْاَرْضُ اَوْ كُلِّمَ بِهِ الْمَوْتٰى ؕ بَلْ لِّلّٰهِ الْاَمْرُ جَمِيْعًا ؕ اَفَلَمْ يَايْئَسِ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اَنْ لَّوْ يَشَآءُ اللّٰهُ لَهَدَى النَّاسَ جَمِيْعًا ؕ وَلَا يَزَالُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا تُصِيْبُهُمْ بِمَا صَنَعُوْا قَارِعَةٌ اَوْ تَحُلُّ قَرِيْبًا مِّنْ دَارِهِمْ حَتّٰى يَاْتِىَ وَعْدُ اللّٰهِ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُخْلِفُ الْمِيْعَادَ‏(31)\nWA LAW ANNAL QURAANAN SUYYERAT BEHIL JEBAALO AW QUTTEA’AT BEHIL ARZO AW KULLEMA BEHIL MAWTAA BAL LILLAAHE MIN JAMEE-A’A A-FALAM YAAYASE LAZEENA AAMANOO AN LAW YASHAAA LAAHO LAHADAA NAASA JAMEE-A’A WA LAA YAZAALU LAZEENA KAFAROO TUSEEBUHUM BEMAA SANAU’OOA QAAREA’ATUN AW TAHULLU QAREEBAA MIN DAAREHIM HATTAA HATTAA WAA’DU LAAHE INNAL LAAHA LAA YUKHLEFUL AL-MEEA’AADA.\nThus have we sent thee amongst a People before whom (long since) have (other) Peoples (gone and) passed away; in order that thou mightest rehearse unto them what We send down unto thee by inspiration; yet do they reject (Him), the Most Gracious! Say: “He is my Lord! There is no god but He! On Him is my trust, and to Him do I turn!” \nوَلَقَدِ اسْتُهْزِئَ بِرُسُلٍ مِّنْ قَبْلِكَ فَاَمْلَيْتُ لِلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا ثُمَّ اَخَذْتُهُمْ فَكَيْفَ كَانَ عِقَابِ‏(32)\nLAQADIS ASTUHZEA BERUSULIN MIN QABLEKA FAAMLAYTU LILLAZEENA KAFAROO SUMMA AAKHAZTUHUM FA-KAYFA KAANA E’EQAABE.\nIf there were a Qur'an with which mountains were moved, or the earth were cloven asunder, or the dead were made to speak, (this would be the one!) But, truly, the command is with Allah in all things! Do not the Believers know, that, had Allah (so) willed, He could have guided all mankind (to the right)? But the Unbelievers, never will disaster cease to seize them for their (ill) deeds, or to settle close to their homes, until the promise of Allah come to pass, for, verily, Allah will not fail in His promise. \nاَفَمَنْ هُوَ قَآئِمٌ عَلٰى كُلِّ نَفْسٍۢ بِمَا كَسَبَتْۚ وَجَعَلُوْالِلّٰهِ شُرَكَآءَ ؕ قُلْ سَمُّوْهُمْؕ اَمْ تُنَبِّئُوْنَهٗ بِمَا لَا يَعْلَمُ فِى الْاَرْضِ اَمْ بِظَاهِرٍ مِّنَ الْقَوْلِؕ بَلْ زُيِّنَ لِلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مَكْرُهُمْ وَصُدُّوْا عَنِ السَّبِيْلِؕ وَمَنْ يُّضْلِلِ اللّٰهُ فَمَا لَهٗ مِنْ هَادٍ‏(33)\nAFAMAWN HOWA QAAEMUN A’LAA KULLE NAFSIM BEMAA KASABAT WAJAA’ALOOALELLAAHE SHORA-KAAA-A QUL SAMMOOHUM AM TUNABEOONAH BEMAA LAA YA’LAMO FIL ARZE AM BEZAAHERIN MENAL AL-QAWLE BAL ZUYYENA LILLAZEENA KAFAROO MAKRUHUM WASUDDOOA A’NIL NIS SABEEL WA MAN YYUZLELE LAAHO FAMAA LAHU MIN HAADIN.\nMocked were (many) messengers before thee: but I granted respite to the unbelievers, and finally I punished them: Then how (terrible) was my requital! \nلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا وَلَعَذَابُ الْاٰخِرَةِ اَشَقُّ ۚ وَمَا لَهُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ مِنْ وَّاقٍ‏(34)\nLAHUM A’ZAABUN FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA LA-A’ZAABUL AAKHERATE AASHAQQU WA MAA LAHUM MENAL LAAHE MIN WWAAQIN.\nIs then He who standeth over every soul (and knoweth) all that it doth, (like any others)? And yet they ascribe partners to Allah. Say: “But name them! is it that ye will inform Him of something he knoweth not on earth, or is it (just) a show of words?” Nay! to those who believe not, their pretence seems pleasing, but they are kept back (thereby) from the path. And those whom Allah leaves to stray, no one can guide. \nمَثَلُ الْجَنَّةِ الَّتِىْ وُعِدَ الْمُتَّقُوْنَ ؕ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ ؕ اُكُلُهَا دَآئِمٌ وَّظِلُّهَا ؕ تِلْكَ عُقْبَى الَّذِيْنَ اتَّقَوْا ۖ  وَّعُقْبَى الْكٰفِرِيْنَ النَّارُ‏(35)\nMASALUL JANNAH LATEE WUE’EDA MUTTAQOON TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO AUKULUHAA DAAEMUN WWAZELLUHAA TILKA U’UQBAA LAZEENA TAQAW WWAU’UQBAA KAAFEREEN TAMASSANAN.\nFor them is a penalty in the life of this world, but harder, truly, is the penalty of the Hereafter: and defender have they none against Allah. \nوَالَّذِيْنَ اٰتَيْنٰهُمُ الْكِتٰبَ يَفْرَحُوْنَ بِمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكَ وَمِنَ الْاَحْزَابِ مَنْ يُّنْكِرُ بَعْضَهٗؕ قُلْ اِنَّمَاۤ اُمِرْتُ اَنْ اَعْبُدَ اللّٰهَ وَلَاۤ اُشْرِكَ بِهٖؕ اِلَيْهِ اَدْعُوْا وَاِلَيْهِ مَاٰبِ‏(36)\nWAL LAZEENA AATAYNAAHOMUL KETAABA YAFRAHOONA BEMAA UNZELA ELAYKA WA MENAN AL-AAHZAABE MAN YYUNKERU BAA’ZAH QUL INNAMAA AN A-A’BODA AN HAAZEHIL BALDATIL LAAHA WA LAA AUSHREKA BEH ELAYHE AADU’OOA WA ELAYHE MAABE.\nThe parable of the Garden which the righteous are promised!- beneath it flow rivers: perpetual is the enjoyment thereof and the shade therein: such is the end of the Righteous; and the end of Unbelievers in the Fire. \nوَكَذٰلِكَ اَنْزَلْنٰهُ حُكْمًا عَرَبِيًّا ؕ وَلَئِنِ اتَّبَعْتَ اَهْوَآءَهُمْ بَعْدَمَا جَآءَكَ مِنَ الْعِلْمِۙ مَا لَكَ مِنَ اللّٰهِ مِنْ وَّلِىٍّ وَّلَا وَاقٍ‏(37)\nWA KAZAALEKA ANZALNAAHO HUKMAWN A’RABIYYAL LA-ENIT TABA’TA AHWAAA-AHUM BA’DA MAA JAAA-AKA MENAL I’LME MAA LAKA MENAL LAAHE MIN WALIYYINW WA LAA WAAQIN.\nThose to whom We have given the Book rejoice at what hath been revealed unto thee: but there are among the clans those who reject a part thereof. Say: “I am commanded to worship Allah, and not to join partners with Him. Unto Him do I call, and unto Him is my return.” \nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا رُسُلًا مِّنْ قَبْلِكَ وَ جَعَلْنَا لَهُمْ اَزْوَاجًا وَّذُرِّيَّةً  ؕ وَمَا كَانَ لِرَسُوْلٍ اَنْ يَّاْتِىَ بِاٰيَةٍ اِلَّا بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِ ؕ لِكُلِّ اَجَلٍ كِتَابٌ‏(38)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA ROSOLAN MIN QABLEKA WA JA-A’LNAA LAHUM AZWAAJANW WWAZURREETAN WA MAA KAANA LE-RASOOLIN AN YAATEYA BE-AAYATIL ILLAA BE-IZNIL LAAHE LEKULLIM ELAA KETAABUN.\nThus have We revealed it to be a judgment of authority in Arabic. Wert thou to follow their (vain) desires after the knowledge which hath reached thee, then wouldst thou find neither protector nor defender against Allah. \nيَمْحُوْا اللّٰهُ مَا يَشَآءُ وَيُثْبِتُ ۖ ۚ وَعِنْدَهٗۤ اُمُّ الْكِتٰبِ‏(39)\nYAMHOOA LAAHO MAA YASHAAA WAYUSBETU WA I’NDAHU AUMMU KETAABE.\nWe did send messengers before thee, and appointed for them wives and children: and it was never the part of a messenger to bring a sign except as Allah permitted (or commanded). For each period is a Book (revealed). \nوَاِنْ مَّا نُرِيَنَّكَ بَعْضَ الَّذِىْ نَعِدُهُمْ اَوْ نَتَوَفَّيَنَّكَ فَاِنَّمَا عَلَيْكَ الْبَلٰغُ وَعَلَيْنَا الْحِسَابُ‏(40)\nWA MAA NUREENNAKA YAWM LAZEE NAE’EDUHUM AW NATAWAFFAYANNAKA FA-INNAMAA A’LAYKA BALAAGHUL WA A’LAYNAA AL-HESAABU.\nAllah doth blot out or confirm what He pleaseth: with Him is the Mother of the Book. \nاَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا اَنَّا نَاْتِى الْاَرْضَ نَنْقُصُهَا مِنْ اَطْرَافِهَا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَحْكُمُ لَا مُعَقِّبَ لِحُكْمِهٖؕ وَهُوَ سَرِيْعُ الْحِسَابِ‏(41)\nAWALAM YARAW ANNAA NAATEAA ARZA NANQUSUHAA MIN AATRAAFEHAA WAL LAAHO YAHKOMO LAA MUA’AQQEBA LEHUKMEH WA HOWA SAREE-U’L HESAAB.\nWhether We shall show thee (within thy life-time) part of what we promised them or take to ourselves thy soul (before it is all accomplished), thy duty is to make (the Message) reach them: it is our part to call them to account. \nوَقَدْ مَكَرَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ فَلِلّٰهِ الْمَكْرُ جَمِيْعًاؕ يَعْلَمُ مَا تَكْسِبُ كُلُّ نَفْسٍؕ وَسَيَعْلَمُ الْكُفّٰرُ لِمَنْ عُقْبَى الدَّارِ‏(42)\nWA QAD MAKARA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM FALILLAAHE AL-MAKRU JAMEEA’AN YA’LAMO MAA TAKSEBU KULLO NAFSIN WASAYAA’LAMU AL-KUFFAARU LEMAN-Y U’UQBAA AD-DAARE.\nSee they not that We gradually reduce the land (in their control) from its outlying borders? (Where) Allah commands, there is none to put back His Command: and He is swift in calling to account. \nوَيَقُوْلُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَسْتَ مُرْسَلًا ؕ قُلْ كَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ شَهِيْدًۢا بَيْنِىْ وَبَيْنَكُمْۙ وَمَنْ عِنْدَهٗ عِلْمُ الْكِتٰبِ‏(43)\nWA YAQOOLO LAZEENA KAFAROO LASTA MURSALAN QUL KAFAA BIL-LAAHE SHAHEEDAA BAYNEE WA BAYNAKUM WA MAN I’NDAHU I’LMUS KETAABE.\nThose before them did (also) devise plots; but in all things the master-planning is Allah's He knoweth the doings of every soul: and soon will the Unbelievers know who gets home in the end. \nبِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nThe Unbelievers say: “No messenger art thou.” Say: “Enough for a witness between me and you is Allah, and such as have knowledge of the Book.” ",
  "merits": "There are 43 verses in this Surah and it is ‘Makki’ though some Mufassireen (those who have written commentaries of the Holy Qur’an) say that the last verse of this Surah was revealed in Madinah. In fact, some even go as far as saying that the whole of this Surah is ‘Madani’ except for two verses.\nThe Holy Prophet (a.s.) has been quoted as saying that whoever recites this Surah will be made from among those who fulfil their promise to Allah (s.w.t.) and they will be given reward which is ten times the number of sins they have committed.\nIt is narrated that Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that if a believer recites this Surah often, he will be taken to Jannah without having to give the long and detailed accounts for his deeds on Earth. He will also be allowed to intercede on behalf of his relatives and friends.\nIf this Surah is written at night, after the time for Isha prayers, under a candle’s light, and then hung outside the door of a tyrant ruler’s palace, then the ruler will perish and so will his control over the people. His army and his supporters will betray him and nobody will listen to him."
